@jpinner sorry I guess you mean "SpdyFrameDecoder" right ? So you say the problem is that if you call:

channel.write(new ...);
channel.write(new ...); 

its possible that the second write will be faster then first if they are executed from different threads ? Thats correct as you would need to schedule the second in a ChannelFutureListener if you want to be sure that its executed after the first.

what you could do is this:

``` java
channel.getChannelPipeline().execute(new Runnable() {
    public void run() {
         channel.write(..)
    }
}
```

This would execute the write request in the IO-Loop/Thread
